CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ constructor of a temporary: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ non-throwing constructor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ noexcept\(noexcept\(int\(\)\)\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ dependent: Throwing: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ dependent: NoThrow: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ constexpr function: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line \d+ noexcept\(noexcept\(may_throw\(\)\)\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.8\] line \d+ noexcept\(noexcept\(wont_throw\(\)\)\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.9\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
noexcept(expression) was not evaluated (taken as non-throwing), and the
noexcept operator did not look at the constructor call held in a
temporary's initializer.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept all assertions but
the last as static_asserts.
